<i>- But won't your wife think--
- Silence!</i>

243
00:10:14,310 --> 00:10:16,310
- She knows nothing
of our love.

244
00:10:18,310 --> 00:10:19,310
- I'm her.

245
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:24,320
<i>- Alex!
- No, don't do that!</i>

246
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,320
You scared the pants off me.
<i>- Ann, my dear.</i>

247
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:28,330
<i>- You, you're glad to see me?
- Yes.</i>

248
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,820
- Sure, as long as
the lights are out.

249
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:32,830
Okay, now beat it.

250
00:10:32,830 --> 00:10:35,330
<i>- I've been wanting a witness
to my great crime.</i>

251
00:10:35,330 --> 00:10:36,330
- Hm.

252
00:10:36,330 --> 00:10:37,330
<i>- Oh.</i>

253
00:10:37,330 --> 00:10:38,340
<i>- Yes.
- Uh-huh.</i>

254
00:10:38,830 --> 00:10:40,330
<i>- I told Mallory
and the others</i>

255
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:43,340
<i>there was a way to induce
a state of suspended animation</i>

256
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:45,340
<i>that couldn't be told
from death,</i>

257
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:46,340
<i>that I could find it.</i>

258
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:47,340
- Uh, play a Kenny G album?

259
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:48,350
<i>- They called me
a dreamer, a fool,</i>

260
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:49,840
<i>but now I have it!</i>

261
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:52,840
<i>And you shall see
and tell them. Come.</i>

262
00:10:52,850 --> 00:10:55,350
- Ah, you've really gone
over the edge this time, prof.

263
00:10:58,350 --> 00:10:59,850
Ooh, I love what you've done
with the place.

264
00:10:59,850 --> 00:11:01,350
- Now what goes on in here?

265
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,860
<i>- You see this disk?
Watch.</i>

266
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:04,360
- This is disk.

267
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:06,860
- Oh, I've seen this one.

268
00:11:06,860 --> 00:11:09,370
- Now, tree, we've never met
before, have we?

269
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,360
Good.

270
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:12,870
- What's he have,
sea monkeys, sea monkeys?

271
00:11:15,870 --> 00:11:16,870
Ah, looks like sea monkeys.

272
00:11:16,870 --> 00:11:18,380
- This is an outrage.

273
00:11:19,370 --> 00:11:20,870
Oosh!

274
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,880
<i>- It will not come to you.</i>

275
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:23,880
- Even spiders have taste.

276
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:24,880
<i>- It will crawl
only to that disk,</i>

277
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:27,380
<i>which I have put there
by the plant.</i>

278
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:30,390
<i>That disk there is magnetized
by a positive ray</i>

279
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:33,390
<i>with my new element,
which is unknown to science.</i>

280
00:11:33,390 --> 00:11:34,390
- Mm-hm.

281
00:11:34,390 --> 00:11:36,390
<i>- And this little spider
carries the magnet.</i>

282
00:11:36,390 --> 00:11:37,900
- Mm-hm, mm-hm.
<i>- And the two--</i>

283
00:11:37,890 --> 00:11:39,390
- Ah, can the balloon juice prop

284
00:11:39,390 --> 00:11:41,390
and get on
with the parlor trick!

285
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,900
- Do that snappy pattern.

286
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:46,900
- Chopper always leaves you
laughing.

287
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:48,910
Ha, ha, ha, ha,
ha, ha, ha.

288
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:50,400
- I can see the string!

289
00:11:52,410 --> 00:11:53,910
- Whoa!

290
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:55,410
- That's my new opening.
What do you think?

291
00:11:55,910 --> 00:11:57,920
<i>- You killed it!
ALEX: <i>No, look.</i>

292
00:11:57,910 --> 00:11:59,410
- Great, you just invented
stop animation.

293
00:11:59,410 --> 00:12:00,410
<i>- Look there.
- ( indistinct )</i>

294
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,420
<i>- --under same circumstances.</i>

295
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:10,430
<i>- It's too bad that Mallory
is not here to see my triumph.</i>

296
00:12:10,430 --> 00:12:11,930
- I have seen it.

297
00:12:11,930 --> 00:12:15,430
<i>- You, you were spying!</i>

298
00:12:16,430 --> 00:12:17,940
<i>- Call it that
if you wish, Alex,</i>

299
00:12:17,930 --> 00:12:19,430
<i>but you made no secret of it.</i>

300
00:12:19,930 --> 00:12:22,430
<i>Now my fear is what are you
going to do with it?</i>

301
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,940
- I'll put it in your shorts,
you little stinker.

302
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:26,940
<i>- Not hand it over
to the government,</i>

303
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:27,950
<i>as you would have me.</i>

304
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,940
<i>- I still think
that would be best.</i>

305
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:32,440
<i>It should be under control
for the good of mankind.</i>

306
00:12:32,450 --> 00:12:34,950
<i>You would still receive credit
for its discovery.</i>

307
00:12:35,450 --> 00:12:37,450
- You just won't be able
to do it any club.

308
00:12:37,450 --> 00:12:40,960
<i>- But possibly--
- Never will I let it go.</i>

309
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:44,960
<i>Already a foreign government
has offered me millions.</i>

310
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,960
<i>Perhaps--
- Thousands.</i>

311
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,470
<i>- I shall sell to them.</i>

312
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,960
<i>- Don't you realize
what a terrific weapon</i>

313
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,960
<i>it would be in the hands
of unscrupulous people?</i>

314
00:12:51,970 --> 00:12:53,470
- Comedy club owners?
<i>- Of course.</i>

315
00:12:53,470 --> 00:12:56,470
<i>That is why they shall
pay me dearly for it.</i>

316
00:12:56,470 --> 00:12:58,480
<i>- Alex, you must not.</i>

317
00:12:58,470 --> 00:13:01,470
<i>- Then it is my duty to
inform the government at once.</i>

318
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,480
<i>- Alex, please!</i>

319
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:03,480
- Ooh, what a look
I'll give you!

320
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,480
- God grant me the serenity
to accept the things

321
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,490
I cannot change and--

322
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,980
<i>- All right.</i>

323
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:14,480
<i>If it is your duty,
do so, by all means,</i>

324
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:18,000
<i>but you will find it
a great mistake.</i>

325
00:13:17,990 --> 00:13:19,990
<i>- What do you mean?</i>

326
00:13:19,990 --> 00:13:21,990
( SINISTER LAUGH BY ALEX )

327
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,500
<i>- You shall soon learn,
all of you!</i>

328
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:26,500
- The power of the dark one.

329
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:29,510
- I'm sorry, but he just
can't help being creepy.

330
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:32,510
- Your prescription
is ready, sir.

331
00:13:32,510 --> 00:13:34,510
<i>- Monk! Monk!
- No.</i>

332
00:13:34,510 --> 00:13:35,510
<i>- Get the devisualizer.</i>

333
00:13:38,010 --> 00:13:39,010
- Ooh.

334
00:13:39,010 --> 00:13:40,010
<i>- Did you carry out
my instructions</i>

335
00:13:40,010 --> 00:13:41,510
<i>regarding the work
to be done on this?</i>

336
00:13:42,020 --> 00:13:43,020
<i>- Yes, sir.</i>

337
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:45,520
- It's an electronic dance bot.
- But I was afraid to use it.

338
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,020
<i>- I'm not afraid!</i>

339
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:48,530
- Haim?
- L'chaim?

340
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:50,520
<i>- They know everything
that I have,</i>

341
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:51,530
<i>but they know nothing
of the devisualizer.</i>

342
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:53,030
- Uh, I think
it goes under the suit.

343
00:13:53,030 --> 00:13:55,030
<i>- It will conceal me
from my enemies.</i>

344
00:13:55,030 --> 00:13:57,030
<i>- I'll stay here, tonight.</i>

345
00:13:57,030 --> 00:13:59,040
<i>Perhaps I can see him again--</i>

346
00:13:59,030 --> 00:14:01,030
- If he'll have me,
the big galoot.

347
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,540
<i>- --and persuade him
from his mad course.</i>

348
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:05,040
<i>- And I'll get in touch
with the government.</i>

349
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,540
<i>I've already talked
with Captain West</i>

350
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:08,050
<i>of the War Department
about Alex.</i>

351
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:09,540
- And I'll give the names
of my colleagues

352
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:10,540
to Senator McCarthy.

353
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:11,550
<i>- No, Ann,
they'll just keep him</i>

354
00:14:11,550 --> 00:14:13,050
<i>and what he has found
under control,</i>

355
00:14:13,050 --> 00:14:15,050
<i>so that he can't misuse it
or dispose of it</i>

356
00:14:15,050 --> 00:14:16,550
<i>to a country that would.</i>

357
00:14:18,550 --> 00:14:19,550
<i>- Ah!</i>

358
00:14:19,550 --> 00:14:22,050
- Oh, oh, I never
should've filled up

359
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,560
on that four-alarm chili.

360
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:25,060
Ooh, excuse me.

361
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:29,060
- Ow.

362
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:32,570
- Oh, burn the file
on the electric dance belt

363
00:14:32,570 --> 00:14:33,570
and pick up my manhood.

364
00:14:33,570 --> 00:14:36,070
It's under the chair.

365
00:14:36,070 --> 00:14:39,080
<i>- You have failed, Monk!</i>

366
00:14:39,070 --> 00:14:40,070
- What do you mean?

367
00:14:40,070 --> 00:14:41,570
I wrote straight, no chaser,
around midnight.

368
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:42,580
I'll take that.

369
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:45,080
<i>- But I will not fail.</i>

370
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:46,580
<i>I cannot.</i>

371
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:49,090
<i>- I'll call, if I need you.
- Goodnight, Ann.</i>

372
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,580
- And I'll go call Roy Cone.

373
00:14:50,590 --> 00:14:51,590
<i>- Goodnight.</i>

374
00:14:54,090 --> 00:14:56,590
- Fits nice, works real--

375
00:14:57,090 --> 00:14:58,600
oh, that's no dance beat.

376
00:14:58,590 --> 00:15:02,090
- Say, that's a pretty good
Patrick Swayze.

377
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:04,600
<i>- It is perfect,
but for a shadow.</i>

378
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:08,110
<i>- But can you come back?
- Surely.</i>

379
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:11,100
<i>- I must come back.
- Hm.</i>

380
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:13,110
- Then I'll go to
Victoria's Secret.

381
00:15:13,110 --> 00:15:14,110
- Heh-heh.

382
00:15:17,110 --> 00:15:18,120
- Think you could steal me

383
00:15:18,110 --> 00:15:19,610
some candy bars
or something someday?

384
00:15:19,610 --> 00:15:21,610
It'd be really cool.
<i>- And now with the phantom,</i>

385
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:24,120
<i>there is nothing
that I cannot do.</i>

386
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:26,120
- If I had you.

387
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:32,620
- Just put some lace
on this dance belt.

388
00:15:32,630 --> 00:15:36,130
Now, will our mystery guest
sign in, please?

389
00:15:37,630 --> 00:15:40,140
- Aw, he gets all
the neat toys.

390
00:15:40,130 --> 00:15:43,130
( SERVO AND CROW
MAKING ROBOTIC NOISES )

391
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:50,140
- Now, if you guys don't mind,

392
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:52,640
I've got a Michelin Man
reading in an hour.

393
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:56,650
ALEX: <i>Nobody can find
our secret workshop</i>

394
00:15:56,650 --> 00:15:59,160
<i>without the Iron Man helping.</i>

395
00:15:59,150 --> 00:16:03,150
- I am Iron Man.

396
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:06,160
<i>- Oh, it conceals so cleverly.</i>

397
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:08,170
<i>Nobody could ever find it.</i>

398
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:10,160
- Unless they're from
the Student Loan Association.

399
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:11,660
<i>- I'll be entirely moved
by morning.</i>

400
00:16:11,670 --> 00:16:12,670
<i>Pack what we need.</i>

401
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:14,670
- Look at all the pizzas
that guy can hold.

402
00:16:20,170 --> 00:16:22,170
- I'll, uh,
just let myself out.

403
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:32,180
- While the cat's away,
the mice will play.

404
00:16:34,690 --> 00:16:37,190
- Oh, I love what you've done
with the place.

405
00:16:37,190 --> 00:16:39,200
- I know,
I get compliments always.

406
00:16:39,190 --> 00:16:40,190
Thank you.

407
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,700
- Oh, sorry, I didn't have
everything packed.

408
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:46,200
Come on,
set that down anywhere.

409
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,700
Can I get you a beer?

410
00:16:51,710 --> 00:16:52,710
- Ah--

411
00:16:54,210 --> 00:16:57,210
now turn your head
and clank.

412
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:06,220
- Hm, wow, this guy really knows
how to get the most

413
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:08,230
out of what limited space
he's got.

414
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:09,220
- I know.

415
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:11,220
He should be in
"Better Dungeons and Gardens."

416
00:17:15,230 --> 00:17:19,240
- My private stock,
Glenfiddich, 30 years old.

417
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:26,740
- Just what science has needed.

418
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:29,250
- He's just blowing off
a little steam there.

419
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:31,740
- Quick, get Vicks
on the phone.

420
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:33,750
I've just invented
the vaporizer.

421
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:34,750
<i>- They must never
know about you,</i>

422
00:17:35,750 --> 00:17:38,760
<i>the source of all my power.</i>

423
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:43,250
( THEME MUSIC PLAYING )

424
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,860
<i>- From what you say,</i>

425
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:48,870
<i>Dr. Zorka has discovered
something very important.</i>

426
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:51,360
<i>- I'm sure he has--
highly dangerous, too.</i>

427
00:17:51,370 --> 00:17:52,870
- Zi umlaut?
- D7?

428
00:17:52,870 --> 00:17:53,870
- Snackmaster?

429
00:17:53,870 --> 00:17:55,870
<i>- Have you made
any search for it?</i>

430
00:17:56,370 --> 00:17:57,880
<i>- No, we thought we'd better
wait until you got here.</i>

431
00:17:57,870 --> 00:17:58,870
- Who are you, anyway?

432
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:00,370
<i>- Let's look
in his laboratory.</i>

433
00:18:01,380 --> 00:18:02,380
<i>- Aren't you going to
take that disk?</i>

434
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:03,880
<i>- Well, uh,
I'll get it later.</i>

435
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,380
<i>I'd hate to have
one of those spiders</i>

436
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:06,380
<i>find it in my pocket.</i>

437
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:09,890
( LAUGHTER )

438
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,880
<i>- Those fools!</i>

439
00:18:11,890 --> 00:18:13,390
<i>Let them search.</i>

440
00:18:13,390 --> 00:18:15,390
- What's he looking at?
<i>- They'll find nothing.</i>

441
00:18:18,390 --> 00:18:20,390
- We'll just break
right in here.

442
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,400
- I really like what
they've done in here

443
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,900
with the pastels
and the, uh, instruments.

444
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:26,900
- Yeah.

445
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,900
<i>- A lot of equipment
seems to have been moved.</i>

446
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,400
- Hm.

447
00:18:31,410 --> 00:18:33,410
<i>- We can talk Rank, a spy ring
guy will be with you.</i>

448
00:18:33,410 --> 00:18:34,410
<i>- But--
- Hm?</i>

449
00:18:34,410 --> 00:18:35,910
<i>- Unseen.
- Oh?</i>

450
00:18:35,910 --> 00:18:38,920
- Next, I'll show you
how to make a bass snagger.

451
00:18:39,410 --> 00:18:41,410
<i>- Your husband
smokes a popular brand.</i>

452
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:42,420
- Columbian.

453
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,420
( LAUGHTER )

454
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:44,920
<i>- He can't stand tobacco.</i>

455
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:46,420
<i>- Well, how about
his assistant?</i>

456
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,930
- He can't stand smoking
his assistant, either.

457
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,920
<i>- She's right.
Zorka worked alone.</i>

458
00:18:52,930 --> 00:18:54,430
- Okay, now,
you be the chauffeur.

459
00:18:54,430 --> 00:18:55,430
I'll be the contessa.

460
00:18:55,430 --> 00:18:58,440
We can play that game again--
ho, ho.

461
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:06,440
<i>- We must be very
careful than ever,</i>

462
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:09,450
<i>that no one discovers the
entrance to our secret garage.</i>

463
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:11,440
- Yeah, right, right, right.
- Whatever.

464
00:19:11,450 --> 00:19:12,950
- Just get in there.

465
00:19:12,950 --> 00:19:14,950
Get into this little
crawl space, you lard butt.

466
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:17,450
Geez. What a pain.

467
00:19:17,450 --> 00:19:18,460
Oh, brother.

468
00:19:18,450 --> 00:19:19,450
<i>- I'll phone headquarters</i>

469
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:21,450
<i>and have his description
broadcast.</i>

470
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:22,460
<i>He'll picked up somewhere;</i>

471
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:24,460
<i>that is, if he still
answers his own description.</i>

472
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:27,460
- I just love
informing on people.

473
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:29,470
<i>- All clear?
- Yes, sir.</i>

474
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:31,960
<i>- Then we will go to meet
the agent of the spy ring.</i>

475
00:19:31,970 --> 00:19:33,470
- Aspiring to what?

476
00:19:34,470 --> 00:19:37,980
<i>- When last seen, he wore
striped trousers,</i>

477
00:19:37,970 --> 00:19:39,970
<i>dark cornard tie
and cutaway coat.</i>

478
