761
00:31:13,070 --> 00:31:17,570
- ♪ There's no one in my life ♪

762
00:31:17,570 --> 00:31:19,580
- Table dancing!
Table dance!

763
00:31:19,570 --> 00:31:20,570
- Whoa, whoa.

764
00:31:21,070 --> 00:31:22,070
- Hey!

765
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:23,580
<i>- ♪ In your arms ♪</i>

766
00:31:23,580 --> 00:31:28,580
- Uh, she must be enforcing
the two-drink minimum, I guess.

767
00:31:28,580 --> 00:31:29,590
- We'd like our check.

768
00:31:29,580 --> 00:31:32,080
<i>- ♪ Don't want to
But I do ♪</i>

769
00:31:32,090 --> 00:31:35,090
- We've got to stop bringing
our business lunches here.

770
00:31:35,090 --> 00:31:37,590
- Let me put my eye in.

771
00:31:37,590 --> 00:31:39,600
What, what is that you say?

772
00:31:39,590 --> 00:31:42,090
What? I can't hear you.

773
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:43,100
Hm?

774
00:31:43,100 --> 00:31:44,100
Oh.

775
00:31:44,100 --> 00:31:45,600
- Uh, do you think
I could get a table

776
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:47,100
in the no singing section?

777
00:31:47,100 --> 00:31:49,110
Is that possible?

778
00:31:49,600 --> 00:31:53,100
<i>- ♪ Or familiar ♪
- Olive.</i>

779
00:31:53,110 --> 00:31:55,110
- So, I was saying
to Brutus the other day--

780
00:31:55,110 --> 00:31:58,110
<i>- ♪ Sharing so patiently ♪</i>

781
00:31:58,610 --> 00:32:00,120
( MIKE AND BOTS COUGHING )

782
00:32:00,110 --> 00:32:02,110
<i>♪ And when you return ♪</i>

783
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:04,120
- So, which navy is he in?

784
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:07,120
- Uh, I think
he's a cab driver. Oh.

785
00:32:07,120 --> 00:32:11,130
<i>- ♪ I'll burn your lips
with kisses ♪</i>

786
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:12,620
- Burn your lips?

787
00:32:12,630 --> 00:32:17,630
- Saigon,
I'm still in Saigon.

788
00:32:17,630 --> 00:32:27,640
<i>- ♪ There's no one in my heart
But you ♪</i>

789
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:29,650
- ♪ And heartburn ♪

790
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:32,640
( APPLAUSE )
- Freebird!

791
00:32:32,650 --> 00:32:36,150
- Whipping post,
whipping post! Woo!

792
00:32:36,150 --> 00:32:37,650
<i>- I was waiting for
three hours last night.</i>

793
00:32:37,650 --> 00:32:39,660
<i>- I did not tell you
I would be there.</i>

794
00:32:40,150 --> 00:32:42,150
- It's a really long song.
<i>- Your eyes said you would.</i>

795
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:44,660
<i>- Aw, but my lips did not.</i>

796
00:32:44,660 --> 00:32:45,660
- My dress said maybe,

797
00:32:45,660 --> 00:32:48,160
but my patella
gave a resounding yes.

798
00:32:48,160 --> 00:32:51,670
<i>- You're sweet,
but dangerous, Mr. Simpson.</i>

799
00:32:51,670 --> 00:32:54,170
<i>- Good, then
I'm making progress.</i>

800
00:32:54,170 --> 00:32:55,170
- Hm.

801
00:32:55,170 --> 00:32:57,670
<i>- Incidentally, Yvonne,
let's stop being so formal.</i>

802
00:32:57,670 --> 00:32:59,180
<i>The name is Bob.</i>

803
00:32:59,170 --> 00:33:01,170
<i>- When I stop being formal,</i>

804
00:33:01,170 --> 00:33:02,670
<i>then it will be
dangerous for you.</i>

805
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:04,180
- Oh!

806
00:33:04,180 --> 00:33:06,680
- Aha, check please.

807
00:33:06,680 --> 00:33:07,680
<i>- I'll give you five minutes.</i>

808
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:09,690
<i>- For what?
- To start running.</i>

809
00:33:11,690 --> 00:33:13,190
<i>- To have another drink.</i>

810
00:33:15,190 --> 00:33:17,190
- Oh, our boyfriend's here.

811
00:33:17,190 --> 00:33:19,200
<i>- I think you have company,
Mr. Simpson.</i>

812
00:33:19,190 --> 00:33:21,190
- And his hat
is more authentic.

813
00:33:22,700 --> 00:33:24,200
- Say, did you take my red
underwear with the big S on it?

814
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:25,700
<i>- I thought
I'd find you in here.</i>

815
00:33:25,700 --> 00:33:28,200
Do you realize we're supposed to
<i>take off in 20 minutes?</i>

816
00:33:28,700 --> 00:33:31,210
<i>- Easy, son, easy.
Have a drink.</i>

817
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:33,200
<i>- We haven't got time.
- We don't fly for Northwest.</i>

818
00:33:33,210 --> 00:33:34,210
<i>- What do you mean
we don't have time?</i>

819
00:33:34,210 --> 00:33:36,210
<i>We've got all the time
in the world.</i>

820
00:33:36,210 --> 00:33:38,210
- Oh, I hate
when he says that.

821
00:33:38,210 --> 00:33:39,220
<i>- Take a look at that.</i>

822
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:44,220
- Hm, look here,
two more pilots arrested.

823
00:33:44,220 --> 00:33:47,220
- Hm, "Famous tennis star
becomes woman complete."

824
00:33:47,220 --> 00:33:48,720
- Hm, ordained minister.

825
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:52,220
<i>- Will of Peter Vanderhorn,
multimillionaire diamond tycoon,</i>

826
00:33:52,230 --> 00:33:53,730
<i>was probated yesterday.</i>

827
00:33:53,730 --> 00:33:54,730
- Hm, sounds painful.

828
00:33:54,730 --> 00:33:56,230
<i>- Provided for reward
of 5,000 pounds sterling</i>

829
00:33:56,230 --> 00:33:59,240
<i>for the discovery of his
daughter, Greta, dead or alive.</i>

830
00:33:59,230 --> 00:34:00,730
<i>She was returning home
by plane</i>

831
00:34:00,730 --> 00:34:02,230
<i>from an American finishing
school, the first day--</i>

832
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:04,240
- Oh, no, no, no. When you
read it, do all the voices.

833
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:05,740
<i>- Last communication
from the navigator</i>

834
00:34:05,740 --> 00:34:08,240
placed the plane somewhere over
<i>the Zambezi territory.</i>

835
00:34:08,240 --> 00:34:10,250
<i>No word of the plane
or any of the passengers</i>

836
00:34:10,240 --> 00:34:11,240
<i>has ever been received.</i>

837
00:34:11,240 --> 00:34:12,740
- Reading my horoscope.
<i>- Well, so what?</i>

838
00:34:12,750 --> 00:34:14,750
<i>Our business is flying
private passengers;</i>

839
00:34:14,750 --> 00:34:16,250
<i>and I don't want
to remind you, son,</i>

840
00:34:16,250 --> 00:34:19,260
<i>but two of them are
waiting for us right now.</i>

841
00:34:19,250 --> 00:34:20,250
<i>- Know what?</i>

842
00:34:20,250 --> 00:34:21,250
<i>Right now,
we're out of business.</i>

843
00:34:21,250 --> 00:34:22,750
- Ssss-- ow!
- Oh!

844
00:34:22,760 --> 00:34:24,260
- Ow.
- Oh, oh!

845
00:34:24,260 --> 00:34:27,760
<i>- Look, Mike, sit down.
- I am sitting.</i>

846
00:34:27,760 --> 00:34:29,770
<i>- There's 5,000 pounds
reward there,</i>

847
00:34:29,760 --> 00:34:31,760
<i>which is about $20,000,</i>

848
00:34:31,770 --> 00:34:34,270
<i>for anyone who finds
Greta Vanderhorn,</i>

849
00:34:34,270 --> 00:34:35,770
<i>and she doesn't
have to be alive.</i>

850
00:34:35,770 --> 00:34:37,770
<i>- You are whacky.
- I'm nutty.</i>

851
00:34:37,770 --> 00:34:39,780
I'm JC Finklehoffer.

852
00:34:39,770 --> 00:34:40,770
<i>- What's been lost
can be found.</i>

853
00:34:40,770 --> 00:34:41,770
<i>- If that were so,</i>

854
00:34:41,780 --> 00:34:43,280
<i>the plane would've been found
a long time ago.</i>

855
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:45,280
<i>- But they weren't able to
send out search planes</i>

856
00:34:45,280 --> 00:34:46,780
<i>while the war was on.</i>

857
00:34:46,780 --> 00:34:47,780
<i>Now that restrictions
have been lifted,</i>

858
00:34:47,780 --> 00:34:50,290
<i>every broken down flyer
on the African coast</i>

859
00:34:50,280 --> 00:34:52,780
<i>will be taking off to look for
the wreckage of that plane,</i>

860
00:34:52,790 --> 00:34:54,790
<i>and we're going to
get there first.</i>

861
00:34:54,790 --> 00:34:57,290
<i>- Who said anything about
getting there at all?</i>

862
00:34:57,290 --> 00:34:58,290
<i>- I did.
- Yeah, he did.</i>

863
00:34:58,290 --> 00:35:01,300
- Yeah, I heard him.
<i>- I hate to remind you, son,</i>

864
00:35:01,290 --> 00:35:03,290
<i>but you're only the junior
partner in this concern.</i>

865
00:35:03,300 --> 00:35:04,300
- I know, Dad.

866
00:35:04,300 --> 00:35:06,300
- I happen to own three-quarters
<i>of that crate, remember?</i>

867
00:35:06,800 --> 00:35:08,300
<i>- Uh, just as if you'd ever
let me forget it.</i>

868
00:35:08,300 --> 00:35:10,810
<i>- Then, come on, Mike.
Time is of the essence.</i>

869
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:11,800
<i>- Yeah, yeah, I know,</i>

870
00:35:11,810 --> 00:35:13,310
<i>just like your old ballet
teacher used to tell you.</i>

871
00:35:13,810 --> 00:35:15,810
- Oh, I deserved that--
good one.

872
00:35:15,810 --> 00:35:17,810
<i>- We've got to load on
some extra tanks of gas.</i>

873
00:35:17,810 --> 00:35:19,320
<i>I think a little trip
in the jungle will do you good.</i>

874
00:35:19,310 --> 00:35:22,310
- Oh, I went
before we got here.

875
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:25,320
- Uh, he's with me.
Excuse us.

876
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:27,320
- There's a man
on the wing of the plane!

877
00:35:27,320 --> 00:35:28,320
- Ah!

878
00:35:29,820 --> 00:35:32,320
- What's a five-letter word
for rum and Diet Pepsi?

879
00:35:32,830 --> 00:35:34,830
<i>- We should hit
Zambezi territory by morning.</i>

880
00:35:34,830 --> 00:35:37,330
- Says you.

881
00:35:37,330 --> 00:35:38,330
- Is that your hand?

882
00:35:38,330 --> 00:35:39,840
Hm.

883
00:35:43,840 --> 00:35:46,340
- I think we just flew
through a dissolve.

884
00:35:53,850 --> 00:35:54,850
- Oh.

885
00:35:58,350 --> 00:36:03,360
Wow, say, these View-Masters
really bring nature to life.

886
00:36:03,360 --> 00:36:04,360
Look at that.

887
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:07,360
That's irr-elephant.

888
00:36:07,860 --> 00:36:09,370
- Hey, I see us up there.

889
00:36:11,870 --> 00:36:13,870
<i>- Okay, boy scout,
how much longer</i>

890
00:36:13,870 --> 00:36:15,870
<i>do you intend to spend
on your good deed?</i>

891
00:36:15,870 --> 00:36:16,870
- Now, I was
in the ballet division.

892
00:36:16,870 --> 00:36:19,380
<i>- It will be a good deed,
if we collect the reward.</i>

893
00:36:19,370 --> 00:36:20,870
<i>- If we collect it.</i>

894
00:36:20,870 --> 00:36:21,870
- You mean those cookies?

895
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:22,880
<i>- Looking for that wreckage
is going to be like</i>

896
00:36:22,880 --> 00:36:23,880
<i>looking for a needle
in a haystack,</i>

897
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:25,380
<i>to coin a phrase.</i>

898
00:36:25,380 --> 00:36:26,380
- Is that yours?

899
00:36:26,380 --> 00:36:27,380
<i>- You go on and coin one,</i>

900
00:36:27,380 --> 00:36:28,380
<i>and if it'll make you feel
any better.</i>

901
00:36:28,380 --> 00:36:29,390
<i>- Nothing's going to make me
feel any better</i>

902
00:36:29,380 --> 00:36:30,880
<i>until we're out of this.</i>

903
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:33,380
Come on, Bob--
- Ah, come clean with me, Frank.

904
00:36:33,390 --> 00:36:34,390
Tell me
you haven't had the urge

905
00:36:34,390 --> 00:36:36,390
to ram this baby
into the ground.

906
00:36:37,890 --> 00:36:41,400
- Hey, a petting zoo.
Now we're at the dells.

907
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:44,900
( THEME MUSIC PLAYING )

908
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,010
<i>- Mike!</i>

909
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,500
- Hm?
- Mike, I think I see something!

910
00:36:52,010 --> 00:36:53,010
<i>Here, take a look.</i>

911
00:36:55,010 --> 00:36:56,010
- Hmph, yeah, that's neat.

912
00:36:56,010 --> 00:36:58,010
Hey, pop in another slide
for me, will you?

913
00:36:58,010 --> 00:36:59,520
<i>- Yeah, could be.</i>

914
00:36:59,510 --> 00:37:01,010
<i>- Well, let's go down
and see.</i>

915
00:37:01,010 --> 00:37:02,010
<i>- Okay.</i>

916
00:37:04,520 --> 00:37:05,520
- Hey, turn back!

917
00:37:05,520 --> 00:37:07,020
We're over Nebraska!

918
00:37:08,020 --> 00:37:10,030
- Did ancient astronauts
land here

919
00:37:10,020 --> 00:37:12,520
millions of years ago?

920
00:37:12,530 --> 00:37:15,030
- Bill, not a crash landing!

921
00:37:15,030 --> 00:37:16,030
- No!

922
00:37:16,030 --> 00:37:19,040
( MIKE AND BOTS SHOUTING )

923
00:37:19,030 --> 00:37:20,530
- Horses and zebra.

924
00:37:21,540 --> 00:37:24,540
- Well, they had to land.
The rubber band is unwound.

925
00:37:30,540 --> 00:37:33,040
- You go ahead, Bob.
You're the boy scout.

926
00:37:33,050 --> 00:37:35,050
Ballet division.

927
00:37:35,550 --> 00:37:36,550
- Look, a tiger!

928
00:37:36,550 --> 00:37:38,050
- What, in Africa?
- Shhh!

929
00:37:38,050 --> 00:37:41,060
- Hey, don't step
in the macumba.

930
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,550
- Nice ensembles
for a couple of guys

931
00:37:42,560 --> 00:37:44,060
who can't remember
to gas up.

932
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:49,070
- Now, how do you run this?

933
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:52,060
- How far away did you say
the wreckage is?

934
00:37:52,070 --> 00:37:53,070
- Uh, that's kind of personal.

935
00:37:53,070 --> 00:37:54,570
- Oh, about a mile.

936
00:37:54,570 --> 00:37:56,070
<i>- North by northeast, right?</i>

937
00:37:56,070 --> 00:37:57,570
- Mm, that was a good movie.

938
00:37:57,570 --> 00:37:59,080
<i>- Keep your eyes peeled, Bob.</i>

939
00:37:59,070 --> 00:38:00,070
<i>Remember, we're not
on the Rue de la Paix.</i>

940
00:38:00,070 --> 00:38:01,070
- I'll go one better.

941
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:02,570
I'll take them clean
out of my sockets,

942
00:38:02,580 --> 00:38:04,080
if you'd like.

943
00:38:04,080 --> 00:38:05,580
- Yeah.

944
00:38:06,580 --> 00:38:08,080
( GROWLING )
- Hello, kitty cat.

945
00:38:08,080 --> 00:38:09,590
( GROWLING )

946
00:38:12,590 --> 00:38:13,590
- Breath mint?

947
00:38:19,090 --> 00:38:21,090
- Springtime,
when a young man's fancies

948
00:38:21,090 --> 00:38:23,090
likely turn to
thoughts of elephants.

949
00:38:23,100 --> 00:38:26,100
- Hi, I'm Satan.
Enjoy the film.

950
00:38:30,100 --> 00:38:32,100
- You're wondering
how we can dominate this,

951
00:38:32,110 --> 00:38:33,110
aren't you, Mike?

