01:05:00,360 --> 01:05:01,860
<i>Didn't you ever
try to get out of here?</i>

1628
01:05:01,860 --> 01:05:03,860
<i>- I used to dream
my way out, Mike.</i>

1629
01:05:03,860 --> 01:05:05,870
- I would take the magic trolley
or click my heels together.

1630
01:05:05,860 --> 01:05:08,360
<i>- I used to dream about home
every night.</i>

1631
01:05:08,370 --> 01:05:11,870
MIKE:     <i>And after that?
- Oh, I gave up dreaming.</i>

1632
01:05:11,870 --> 01:05:13,870
<i>It was hopeless to try
and penetrate the jungle.</i>

1633
01:05:13,870 --> 01:05:14,880
- Hm.

1634
01:05:14,870 --> 01:05:16,370
<i>- I used to have the natives
take me out</i>

1635
01:05:16,370 --> 01:05:18,370
<i>on what you might call
hunting expeditions,</i>

1636
01:05:18,380 --> 01:05:19,880
<i>but they led nowhere.</i>

1637
01:05:19,880 --> 01:05:22,880
- Then I just had a hamburger
with some French fried potatoes.

1638
01:05:22,880 --> 01:05:24,390
GRETA:
<i>I know.</i>

1639
01:05:24,380 --> 01:05:25,880
<i>And my only hold on them</i>

1640
01:05:25,880 --> 01:05:29,380
<i>depends on their belief
that I'm a goddess.</i>

1641
01:05:29,390 --> 01:05:32,390
- And so Leona Helmsley's
empire was built.

1642
01:05:32,390 --> 01:05:34,400
<i>- --if we're to get
out of here alive.</i>

1643
01:05:34,390 --> 01:05:37,390
<i>- You must tell Bob
not to make any false moves.</i>

1644
01:05:37,400 --> 01:05:38,400
- Like killing people.

1645
01:05:38,400 --> 01:05:40,400
GRETA:  <i>He's got to be patient
until tomorrow morning.</i>

1646
01:05:40,400 --> 01:05:42,400
<i>- Are you sure
you can trust Wanama?</i>

1647
01:05:42,400 --> 01:05:43,900
GRETA<i>Wanama would do
anything for me.</i>

1648
01:05:43,900 --> 01:05:45,410
- Wanama's phenomenal.

1649
01:05:45,400 --> 01:05:47,400
- She's the only one I can trust
<i>to lead us out of the jungle.</i>

1650
01:05:47,410 --> 01:05:48,410
<i>- Bob has a hand compass.</i>

1651
01:05:48,410 --> 01:05:49,910
- And some
French fried potatoes.

1652
01:05:50,410 --> 01:05:52,910
- That will come in handy, too,
<i>in case anything goes wrong.</i>

1653
01:05:52,910 --> 01:05:56,420
<i>I, uh, think
you'd better leave now.</i>

1654
01:05:56,410 --> 01:05:57,910
<i>- You always say
something like that</i>

1655
01:05:57,920 --> 01:05:59,920
<i>just when I'm
beginning to enjoy myself.</i>

1656
01:05:59,920 --> 01:06:01,420
- Then I've gotta wait a few
minutes before I can leave.

1657
01:06:01,420 --> 01:06:03,920
<i>- It's best.
- Well, that's life.</i>

1658
01:06:08,930 --> 01:06:10,930
<i>Here, what is this?
Where'd you get this?</i>

1659
01:06:10,930 --> 01:06:12,430
<i>- Wanama made it for me.</i>

1660
01:06:12,430 --> 01:06:14,940
- Hm, world's greatest grandma.

1661
01:06:14,930 --> 01:06:16,930
<i>- Hey, where did Wanama
get the stuff</i>

1662
01:06:16,940 --> 01:06:17,940
<i>she carved this from?</i>

1663
01:06:17,940 --> 01:06:19,440
<i>- On the outskirts
of the village.</i>

1664
01:06:19,440 --> 01:06:21,440
<i>Why?
- Why?</i>

1665
01:06:21,440 --> 01:06:22,940
- Wanama's working through
a lot of pain, isn't she?

1666
01:06:22,940 --> 01:06:24,950
<i>- Do you know what this is?
No, I guess you don't.</i>

1667
01:06:24,940 --> 01:06:26,940
<i>I saw something
just like this in Colorado.</i>

1668
01:06:26,950 --> 01:06:27,950
<i>- Well, what is it?</i>

1669
01:06:27,950 --> 01:06:29,450
<i>- Unless I'm crazy,
it's chronatite.</i>

1670
01:06:29,950 --> 01:06:31,450
<i>Of course, that wouldn't mean
anything to you, either.</i>

1671
01:06:31,450 --> 01:06:32,450
<i>Chronatite
is stuff that they use</i>

1672
01:06:32,450 --> 01:06:34,460
<i>in the manufacture
of atomic energy.</i>

1673
01:06:34,450 --> 01:06:35,450
- Saps all your power,

1674
01:06:35,450 --> 01:06:37,450
if you're a visitor
from a foreign planet.

1675
01:06:37,460 --> 01:06:39,460
<i>- Are you serious?
- Of course, I'm serious.</i>

1676
01:06:39,460 --> 01:06:40,960
<i>- Look, Bob knows a lot
about this kind of thing.</i>

1677
01:06:40,960 --> 01:06:42,460
<i>Do you mind
if I show it to him?</i>

1678
01:06:42,460 --> 01:06:43,460
<i>- Not if you want to.</i>

1679
01:06:43,460 --> 01:06:44,470
- Yeah, you can take
target practice on it.

1680
01:06:44,460 --> 01:06:45,460
<i>- If it is chronatite,</i>

1681
01:06:45,460 --> 01:06:46,460
<i>we'll organize
our own expedition</i>

1682
01:06:46,460 --> 01:06:48,460
<i>and come back for it.</i>

1683
01:06:48,470 --> 01:06:50,970
<i>- Provided we get
out of here alive, Mike.</i>

1684
01:06:50,970 --> 01:06:54,480
- ♪ Wa-wa-wa-wa-wa ♪

1685
01:06:54,470 --> 01:06:57,470
( THEME MUSIC PLAYING )

1686
01:07:06,320 --> 01:07:07,820
- Hm, tastes like grandpa.

1687
01:07:10,820 --> 01:07:12,320
It's chronatite all right.

1688
01:07:12,320 --> 01:07:13,820
<i>- You sure?
- I'd stake my life on it.</i>

1689
01:07:13,830 --> 01:07:15,330
- That's already
in the kitty, Bob.

1690
01:07:15,330 --> 01:07:16,330
<i>- I don't know
what it means to you,</i>

1691
01:07:16,330 --> 01:07:18,330
<i>but personally I've had my eye
on a ranch in Colorado</i>

1692
01:07:18,330 --> 01:07:19,330
<i>ever since I was a kid.</i>

1693
01:07:19,330 --> 01:07:21,340
<i>- Hm.
- Oh, yeah, like I care.</i>

1694
01:07:25,340 --> 01:07:26,840
<i>- Nugara is still on guard.</i>

1695
01:07:27,340 --> 01:07:29,340
<i>Our best chance is to make
a break for it just before dawn.</i>

1696
01:07:29,340 --> 01:07:30,340
<i>- Oh, wait a minute.</i>

1697
01:07:30,340 --> 01:07:32,350
<i>Greta's worked out
a plan for us.</i>

1698
01:07:32,340 --> 01:07:34,340
- Hey, when did you start
calling her Greta?

1699
01:07:34,350 --> 01:07:35,350
- She told me
to call her goddess.

1700
01:07:35,850 --> 01:07:36,350
<i>- There's no
getting through that jungle</i>

1701
01:07:36,850 --> 01:07:38,350
<i>without being slowed down
by a dame.</i>

1702
01:07:38,350 --> 01:07:39,350
<i>- Well, if we get through--</i>

1703
01:07:39,350 --> 01:07:40,860
<i>and I doubt very much
if we can--</i>

1704
01:07:40,850 --> 01:07:42,850
<i>Oolonga would be a cinch
to blame her.</i>

1705
01:07:42,850 --> 01:07:43,850
<i>Have you ever
stopped to think</i>

1706
01:07:43,860 --> 01:07:45,360
<i>what those natives
might do to her?</i>

1707
01:07:45,360 --> 01:07:46,360
- Oh, yeah.
<i>- So what?</i>

1708
01:07:46,360 --> 01:07:48,360
<i>That's her lookout.
She's the white goddess.</i>

1709
01:07:48,360 --> 01:07:50,870
<i>She can figure
a way out of this.</i>

1710
01:07:50,860 --> 01:07:52,860
<i>- Supposed they kill her?</i>

1711
01:07:52,860 --> 01:07:53,860
<i>- We don't have to
bring her back alive</i>

1712
01:07:53,870 --> 01:07:55,370
<i>to collect the reward.</i>

1713
01:07:55,370 --> 01:07:56,870
<i>And besides,
that's peanuts</i>

1714
01:07:56,870 --> 01:07:57,870
<i>alongside what
we'll collect on this.</i>

1715
01:07:57,870 --> 01:07:59,370
- Hey, your horns
are showing, Bob.

1716
01:07:59,370 --> 01:08:01,380
- Where are you going?
- I'm taking this back to Greta.

1717
01:08:01,370 --> 01:08:03,370
<i>Bob, I'm going to be kind
to you.</i>

1718
01:08:03,380 --> 01:08:04,380
- I'm going to put you to sleep.

1719
01:08:04,380 --> 01:08:06,380
<i>- The spot you're on
has twisted your mind.</i>

1720
01:08:06,380 --> 01:08:08,380
<i>Nobody can be
that much of a heel!</i>

1721
01:08:08,380 --> 01:08:10,380
- But I can.
- I can; really, I can.

1722
01:08:10,380 --> 01:08:13,390
- Sure, you can.
- No, I can, really.

1723
01:08:13,390 --> 01:08:14,890
- I am a heel.
- How about a heel like he is?

1724
01:08:14,890 --> 01:08:16,890
- Why are they looking at me?
Get that camera off of me.

1725
01:08:16,890 --> 01:08:17,890
- I'm a heel.

1726
01:08:17,890 --> 01:08:19,390
- We'll be back
right after this.

1727
01:08:19,390 --> 01:08:21,900
- I'm still a heel.
- Such a heel.

1728
01:08:23,400 --> 01:08:25,400
<i>- I appreciate the fact
that I can't leave this hole,</i>

1729
01:08:25,400 --> 01:08:27,400
<i>but is there any reason
why I can't have some water?</i>

1730
01:08:27,400 --> 01:08:28,400
<i>- Water?</i>

1731
01:08:28,400 --> 01:08:30,400
<i>- If it isn't
too much trouble.</i>

1732
01:08:30,400 --> 01:08:31,410
<i>- Wanama.</i>

1733
01:08:32,900 --> 01:08:34,400
<i>Bring white devil water.</i>

1734
01:08:34,410 --> 01:08:35,910
<i>- Water.</i>

1735
01:08:35,910 --> 01:08:37,410
<i>- Yeah, bring a lot of it,
and don't forget the ice.</i>

1736
01:08:37,410 --> 01:08:39,410
<i>- Ice?</i>

1737
01:08:39,410 --> 01:08:40,410
<i>- Skip it.
- Skip it?</i>

1738
01:08:40,410 --> 01:08:42,920
- And, Wanama, bring it inside.
- Inside?

1739
01:08:42,910 --> 01:08:44,410
<i>- It's hotter than blazes
out here.</i>

1740
01:08:44,420 --> 01:08:45,420
- Blazes?

1741
01:08:46,920 --> 01:08:48,420
<i>- I've arranged to send
all the natives out</i>

1742
01:08:48,420 --> 01:08:50,420
<i>on hunting expeditions
early tomorrow morning.</i>

1743
01:08:50,420 --> 01:08:52,930
<i>That will enable us
to travel by daylight.</i>

1744
01:08:52,920 --> 01:08:54,420
<i>- What about Nugara?</i>

1745
01:08:54,430 --> 01:08:56,430
<i>- You'll have to tie him up,
but I don't want him hurt.</i>

1746
01:08:56,430 --> 01:08:57,430
<i>Understand?</i>

1747
01:08:57,430 --> 01:08:58,430
<i>- You mean
you don't trust him?</i>

1748
01:08:58,430 --> 01:09:01,940
<i>- Oh, I don't dare.
After all, he is a Zambezi.</i>

1749
01:09:01,930 --> 01:09:04,430
<i>These natives are very
peculiar and childlike.</i>

1750
01:09:04,440 --> 01:09:06,440
- They don't even shoot things
they don't understand.

1751
01:09:06,440 --> 01:09:07,940
<i>- even if he knew
what we were up to.</i>

1752
01:09:07,940 --> 01:09:09,940
<i>- Well, what makes you think
you can trust Wanama?</i>

1753
01:09:09,940 --> 01:09:10,950
<i>- Oh, I know I can.</i>

1754
01:09:10,940 --> 01:09:12,940
<i>After all, she's been
my constant companion</i>

1755
01:09:12,940 --> 01:09:14,940
<i>for six years.</i>

1756
01:09:14,950 --> 01:09:16,450
<i>- Tell me, Wanama.</i>

1757
01:09:16,950 --> 01:09:18,450
<i>You know the jungle
pretty well, don't you?</i>

1758
01:09:18,450 --> 01:09:19,950
- Oh, I get around.
<i>- Oh, sure.</i>

1759
01:09:19,950 --> 01:09:22,460
- Are you really an astronaut?
<i>- Me very dumb.</i>

1760
01:09:22,950 --> 01:09:24,450
<i>- I guess you are at that.</i>

1761
01:09:24,460 --> 01:09:26,960
<i>Did you ever wonder
where Mata Greta came from?</i>

1762
01:09:26,960 --> 01:09:30,970
- Ah, she's a temp, right?
-  <i>The gods sent Mata Greta.</i>

1763
01:09:30,960 --> 01:09:34,960
<i>- Is that what she told you?
- Oh, no, but me know.</i>

1764
01:09:34,970 --> 01:09:36,970
<i>Everybody know.</i>

1765
01:09:36,970 --> 01:09:39,470
<i>- You love Mata Greta
very much, don't you?</i>

1766
01:09:39,470 --> 01:09:42,480
<i>- Oh, sure.</i>

1767
01:09:42,470 --> 01:09:44,970
<i>Everybody love Mata Greta.</i>

1768
01:09:44,980 --> 01:09:45,980
<i>- Then you'd want to help her,</i>

1769
01:09:45,980 --> 01:09:48,480
<i>if she needed you,
wouldn't you?</i>

1770
01:09:48,480 --> 01:09:49,980
-  <i>Help Mata Greta?
- Come on, get to the point!</i>

1771
01:09:49,980 --> 01:09:52,490
Cut to the chase!
<i>( indistinct ) Mata Greta?</i>

1772
01:09:52,480 --> 01:09:54,980
<i>- It will,
if we don't help her.</i>

1773
01:09:54,990 --> 01:09:56,990
<i>- Okay, what about the rifles.</i>

1774
01:09:56,990 --> 01:09:59,990
<i>- I, uh, I had to
have them destroyed.</i>

1775
01:09:59,990 --> 01:10:02,000
<i>The natives thought
they were weapons of evil.</i>

1776
01:10:01,990 --> 01:10:03,990
- Heh-heh, they're kind of cute,
so leave me.

1777
01:10:04,000 --> 01:10:06,000
( CHUCKLING )

1778
01:10:06,000 --> 01:10:08,000
<i>- Yes, the jungle is infested
with wild animals.</i>

1779
01:10:08,000 --> 01:10:09,000
- Ha, so am I?

1780
01:10:09,000 --> 01:10:10,000
<i>- Well, if we should
get in a spot,</i>

1781
01:10:10,000 --> 01:10:12,510
<i>you can always exert
your powers, white goddess.</i>

1782
01:10:12,500 --> 01:10:15,000
- Oh-ho, that's rich.
Kill him.

1783
01:10:15,010 --> 01:10:18,010
<i>- Mike, do you think
you could get</i>

1784
01:10:18,010 --> 01:10:20,010
<i>Bob's revolver
away from him?</i>

1785
01:10:20,010 --> 01:10:23,020
<i>I don't trust him.
- No, he'd never give it up.</i>

1786
01:10:23,010 --> 01:10:25,010
<i>- Then we'll just have to
take our chances.</i>

1787
01:10:25,020 --> 01:10:26,020
<i>- Now, don't worry.</i>

1788
01:10:26,020 --> 01:10:27,520
- I'm the man of steel,

1789
01:10:27,520 --> 01:10:29,520
stop bullets,
the whole nine yards.

1790
01:10:29,520 --> 01:10:30,520
<i>- You know,
it would serve him right,</i>

1791
01:10:31,020 --> 01:10:32,020
<i>if we'd turn him over</i>

1792
01:10:32,020 --> 01:10:34,520
<i>to the tender mercies
of Oolonga the witch doctor.</i>

1793
01:10:34,530 --> 01:10:36,530
<i>- Here, here,
we couldn't do that.</i>

1794
01:10:36,530 --> 01:10:38,530
- Let me just
patronize you a bit.

1795
01:10:38,530 --> 01:10:41,540
<i>- You know, Mike, I think
you're absolutely right.</i>

1796
01:10:41,530 --> 01:10:43,530
<i>He's undoubtedly
become unbalanced</i>

1797
01:10:43,540 --> 01:10:44,540
<i>by all that's happened.</i>

1798
01:10:44,540 --> 01:10:46,040
- Yeah, he's not thinking
as clearly

1799
01:10:46,040 --> 01:10:47,040
as when he shot that guy.

1800
01:10:47,040 --> 01:10:49,040
<i>- We'll have to watch him
very closely.</i>

1801
01:10:49,040 --> 01:10:51,550
<i>- Relax, goddess, relax.</i>

1802
01:10:53,040 --> 01:10:54,540
<i>- What's the matter, Wanama?</i>

1803
01:10:54,550 --> 01:10:56,050
- Yeah, kitten,
why the long face?

1804
01:10:56,050 --> 01:10:59,050
<i>- Me want to talk
Mata Greta alone.</i>

1805
01:10:59,050 --> 01:11:02,060
<i>- That's all right.
You may speak.</i>

1806
01:11:02,050 --> 01:11:03,050
<i>He's our friend.</i>

1807
01:11:03,050 --> 01:11:05,550
<i>- He friend white devil, too.</i>

1808
01:11:05,560 --> 01:11:09,060
<i>Please, Mata Greta, Wanama
want to speak with you alone!</i>

1809
01:11:09,560 --> 01:11:10,560
- What's the matter Wanama?

1810
01:11:10,560 --> 01:11:13,570
<i>- I have a feeling
this concerns the both of us.</i>

1811
01:11:13,570 --> 01:11:15,570
- Hm.
<i>- What happened, Wanama?</i>

1812
01:11:15,570 --> 01:11:17,570
<i>Were you with white devil?</i>

1813
01:11:17,570 --> 01:11:18,570
- Or should I get out
the anatomically correct doll?

1814
01:11:18,570 --> 01:11:20,070
<i>- Are you afraid
to tell me what happened?</i>

1815
01:11:20,070 --> 01:11:21,580
<i>- No.</i>

1816
01:11:21,570 --> 01:11:25,070
<i>Please, me want to talk
Mata Greta alone.</i>

1817
01:11:25,080 --> 01:11:28,080
<i>- Mata Greta wants you
to speak now.</i>

1818
01:11:28,080 --> 01:11:29,580
- Get on with it, please!

1819
01:11:30,080 --> 01:11:32,590
<i>- White devil want me
take him through jungle.</i>

1820
01:11:32,580 --> 01:11:33,580
<i>- Alone?</i>

1821
01:11:33,590 --> 01:11:35,590
<i>- He say that way
we help Mata Greta,</i>

1822
01:11:35,590 --> 01:11:37,090
<i>but Wanama don't believe.</i>

1823
01:11:37,090 --> 01:11:39,590
<i>- You didn't tell him
you were coming here, did you?</i>

1824
01:11:39,590 --> 01:11:42,600
<i>- Oh, no.
Wanama, Wanama dumb.</i>

1825
01:11:42,590 --> 01:11:44,590
- Wanama dumb--
doo-doo-doo-doo-doo.

1826
01:11:44,600 --> 01:11:46,100
Wanama dumb--
doo-doo-doo-doo.

1827
01:11:46,100 --> 01:11:47,100
<i>- Be careful, Mike.</i>

1828
01:11:52,100 --> 01:11:55,100
- So, did you do it?

1829
01:11:55,110 --> 01:11:58,610
<i>- Mata Greta.</i>

1830
01:11:58,610 --> 01:12:01,620
<i>Mata Greta love him?</i>

1831
01:12:01,610 --> 01:12:03,610
- Isn't there a magazine
devoted to this?

1832
01:12:03,620 --> 01:12:05,120
- Oh.

1833
01:12:07,120 --> 01:12:08,120
MIKE:
<i>I'll take that, Bob.</i>

1834
01:12:10,120 --> 01:12:12,130
<i>- Are you daffy?
- No, I'm Porky.</i>

1835
01:12:12,120 --> 01:12:13,120
You're Daffy.
Remember?

1836
01:12:13,120 --> 01:12:14,120
<i>- I don't think so.</i>

1837
01:12:14,130 --> 01:12:16,630
<i>We're pulling out
tomorrow morning,</i>

1838
01:12:16,630 --> 01:12:18,130
<i>and Greta and I both decided
that it would be better</i>

1839
01:12:18,130 --> 01:12:20,130
<i>if I packed the artillery
on this little safari.</i>

1840
01:12:20,130 --> 01:12:21,140
- Yeah, see?

1841
01:12:21,130 --> 01:12:23,630
<i>- Oh, you and Greta decided,
did you?</i>

